      area 0
       network x.x.x.x x.x.x.x  # Configure your OSPF network
      bgp-ls enable  # Enable BGP-LS to export OSPF topology
     ```

### 2. **Configure BGP and Enable Link-State Address Family**
   ```bash
   bgp <LOCAL_AS_NUM>  # Replace with your router's AS number (e.g., 100)
    router-id x.x.x.x  # Optional: Set a BGP Router ID
    peer 192.168.55.66 as-number <PEER_AS_NUM>  # Specify peer's AS number
    #
    link-state-family  # Enter BGP-LS address family
     peer 192.168.55.66 enable  # Activate BGP-LS with the peer
