How to configure Huawei routers to allow BGP IPv6 unicast routes to consider sub-optimal external paths when the preferred IBGP route exists?


To configure Huawei routers to allow BGP IPv6 unicast routes to consider sub-optimal external (EBGP) paths when a preferred IBGP route exists, you can use BGP Fast ReRoute (FRR) to install backup paths. Here's how to do it:

### Step-by-Step Configuration:
1. **Create a Route-Policy to Mark EBGP Routes as Backup:**
   ```bash
   route-policy ebgp-backup permit node 10
    apply frr backup
   ```
   This policy marks matched routes (EBGP) as backup paths.

2. **Apply the Route-Policy in BGP IPv6 Address Family:**
   ```bash
   bgp <AS-number>
    ipv6-family unicast
     frr
      policy ebgp-backup
   ```
   Replace `<AS-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number.

