How to configure a Huawei router to advertise BGP routes with ELC-type entropy labels to peer 192.168.5.5 using padding value AABBCCDDEEFF0011?


To configure a Huawei router to advertise BGP routes with ELC-type entropy labels to peer 192.168.5.5 using the specified padding value, follow these steps:

1. **Enable MPLS and Configure Entropy Label Parameters**:
   ```plaintext
   <Router> system-view
   [Router] mpls lsr-id 1.1.1.1  # Set the MPLS LSR ID
   [Router] mpls
   [Router-mpls] entropy-label enable
   [Router-mpls] entropy-label padding 64 AABBCCDDEEFF0011
   [Router-mpls] quit
   ```
   - `entropy-label enable`: Activates entropy label capability.
   - `entropy-label padding 64 AABBCCDDEEFF0011`: Sets the 64-bit (8-byte) padding value in hex (AABBCCDDEEFF0011).

2. **Configure BGP Peer and Advertise Entropy Labels**:
   ```plaintext
   [Router] bgp 100
   [Router-bgp] peer 192.168.5.5 as-number 100
   [Router-bgp] peer 192.168.5.5 connect-interface LoopBack0  # Or relevant interface
   [Router-bgp] ipv4-family unicast
   [Router-bgp-ipv4] peer 192.168.5.5 enable
   [Router-bgp-ipv4] peer 192.168.5.5 label-route-capability  # Enable BGP Labeled Unicast (BGP-LU)
   [Router-bgp-ipv4] peer 192.168.5.5 advertise-entropy-label elc
   [Router-bgp-ipv4] quit
   [Router-bgp] quit
   ```
   - `label-route-capability`: Enables BGP-LU to exchange labeled routes.
   - `advertise-entropy-label elc`: Advertises entropy labels with ELC capability to the peer.

**Verification**:
- Check BGP peer status:
