```

### 2. **Apply the Route-Policy to the BGP Peer:**
Enter BGP configuration and apply the policy to the peer in the outbound direction.

```bash
bgp <your_as_number>  # Replace with your BGP AS number
peer 192.168.50.25 as-number <peer_as_number>  # Specify peer's AS number
ipv4-family unicast  # Enter IPv4 address family view
 peer 192.168.50.25 enable  # Enable the peer if not already active
 peer 192.168.50.25 route-policy bgp_filter export  # Apply policy to outgoing routes
```

